  "decisions": [
    "Keep existing Full pass order (62 passes). No Fast pipeline change.",
    "Retain exact equality support in existing opt-in branch-ranges pass.",
    "Retain bounded merge load reuse and constant memcpy lowering in existing pipelines.",
    "Reject one-round/three-round late cleanup and earlier bulk cleanup schedules for default use.",
    "The earlier schedule benefits yyjson but is substantially worse on interpreter workloads.",
    "Same-schedule frozen-compiler control shows yyjson gains largely come from scheduling existing passes, not uniquely from new pointer facts.",
    "Pugixml advances to llvm.memcpy parameter/return ABI attribute rejection; no full C++ application claim."
  ],
  "method": "Paired elapsed-time ratios, median of per-round candidate/baseline ratios. Bootstrap 95% percentile interval from 5000 resamples; seed19. Two warmups; 11 runtime rounds for new apps, 7 for older apps; compile rounds3 and1 respectively. Shared preprocessed C to assembly/object, preprocessing/linking excluded. Runtime includes startup; no LTO/PGO. Same-byte Clang control retained in raw reports.",
  "limits": [
    "ARM native execution only; x86 direct/text object consistency is not native validation.",
    "Single host, short local campaigns. Small changes and narrow intervals are not universal guarantees.",
    "Two C++ fixture optimization levels produce identical LLVM IR; do not count them as independent source diversity.",
    "Aggregate transport supports exact two-i64 parameters only, not arbitrary aggregate SSA/returns."
  ],
